## CRIT findings (must fix this round)

### CRIT-001 (correctness lens) — prior-green-CI safety check is non-functional

**Bug:** the new safety check in scripts/enable-required-check.sh queries `repos/<owner>/<repo>/commits/<default-branch-HEAD-sha>/check-runs` for `policy-check / scp/policy-check` with conclusion=success. But adopter wrappers use `on: pull_request:` only — check runs are keyed to PR head SHAs, NOT the default-branch merge commit. So the query permanently returns empty; the foot-gun guard never fires; the `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag is always required. Also the 60-day window from DISPATCH-NOTE is absent from the implementation.

**Fix:** replace the per-commit check-runs query with a workflow-runs API call filtered by workflow name + 60-day date window:
1. Resolve the workflow ID by querying `gh api repos/${REPO}/actions/workflows --jq '.workflows[] | select(.name == "policy-check") | .id'`. Save to `WORKFLOW_ID`.
2. If `WORKFLOW_ID` is empty (no `policy-check` workflow registered), exit 1 with a clear error.
3. Compute the 60-day cutoff ISO-8601 timestamp via python3 (BSD-date portability — `python3 -c "import datetime; print((datetime.datetime.now(datetime.timezone.utc) - datetime.timedelta(days=60)).strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'))"`).
4. Query `gh api 'repos/${REPO}/actions/runs?workflow_id=${WORKFLOW_ID}&status=success&created=>=<cutoff>'` and check whether the result has any runs.
5. If empty: exit 1 with the existing error message `ERROR: target <owner>/<repo> has no successful policy-check workflow runs in the last 60 days; refuse to enable required-check before wrapper has green-CI'd at least once. Override with --i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci if you accept the risk.`
6. If non-empty: proceed.

The `--i-understand-this-repo-has-no-prior-green-ci` flag continues to bypass this check; restore-mode continues to skip this check.

