### MAJ-BYPASS-006 (safety lens) — ADOPT-001 §12.8 Gate 3 has no prerequisite check that Gate 2 was completed

**Bug:** Gate 3 (re-enable) has no prerequisite check that Gate 2 (SHA pin to known-good release tag) was completed. The procedure describes three sequential gates but nothing in the procedure or tooling prevents an operator from executing Gate 1 (disable via --restore) → skip Gate 2 → execute Gate 3 (re-enable) immediately, leaving the cascade re-armed while the federation primitive is still defective.

**Fix:** amend docs/adoption/ADOPT-001-project-onboarding.md §12.8 Gate 3 to add an explicit numbered prerequisite check at the start:
